Notebook[{
Cell["CubeMomentCornerQuadrature", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"a5320c8d-93f2-4aa7-9a98-6831a1ed87f3"],

Cell["\<\
ADAPTIVE CUBATURE AT THE CORNER OF THE OCTANT, AGAINST THE CLOSED FORMS\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"1814bfc9-f39d-43ac-82d5-f120a7c3f75a"],

Cell["\<\
The scalar moments of the cube with fewer than two derivatives on the kernel,
    E[-1; d; w] = int_cube x_w d_d (1/r) d^3x ,   D = |d| <= 1,
are ordinary integrals: the integrand is bounded at r = 0 for these weights \
but not smooth there.
CubeMomentHigherGrades.wl checks every non-vanishing index class of the \
grades (1,3), (0,4) and (1,5)
(9, 6 and 18 classes) against numerical integration, 8 times the octant [0, \
1/2]^3, where the
singular point sits at a corner of the region.  This file measures what the \
integration settings do
there, class by class, against the closed forms of CubeMomentCore.wl:\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"c805e232-a10d-4a16-81d6-78130d6dcdca"],

Cell["\<\
  plain      Method -> \"GlobalAdaptive\" (the check's setting until 30 \
October 2026)
  duffy      Method -> {\"GlobalAdaptive\", \"SingularityHandler\" -> \
\"DuffyCoordinates\"} (its setting now)
  maxerr     Method -> {\"GlobalAdaptive\", \"MaxErrorIncreases\" -> 10^4}, \
on the classes where plain warns\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"cec8a957-a3a7-4064-adf4-8d6ea258f7b1"],

Cell["\<\
all with PrecisionGoal 10, AccuracyGoal 12, MaxRecursion 25, WorkingPrecision \
20.  Each integration runs quietly: the messages it would issue are recorded, \
by name, as part of the result.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f7d7afc6-959a-4fe8-a028-f1c2cd41e49b"],

Cell["\<\
Run:  wolframscript -file Mathematica/CubeMomentCornerQuadrature.wl\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eb7d1cb3-2855-4cd8-bf17-e98d4168ea3b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

